; On another thread, exit asks the main thread to exit; what the console
; reads after it never runs. Unload actions run in clean-up tasks, as for
; every exit.
> (import (place))
> (begin (join-task (fork-task (lambda (restore) (exit) (display "never")))) (void))
configuration unloading
unloading in a task
keeper unloading
> (display "never runs")
